u sure you want to remove the %1 <nobr><b>%2</b></nobr> from the list of known media?";}s:12:"Attached to:";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:12:"Attached to:";}s:19:"Choose medium type:";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:19:"Choose medium type:";}s:7:"Copy...";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:7:"Copy...";}s:12:"Description:";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:12:"Description:";}s:87:"Do you want to delete the storage unit of the virtual hard disk <nobr><b>%1</b></nobr>?";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:87:"Do you want to delete the storage unit of the virtual hard disk <nobr><b>%1</b></nobr>?";}s:7:"Encoded";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:7:"Encoded";}s:12:"Floppy disks";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:12:"Floppy disks";}s:7:"Format:";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:7:"Format:";}s:10:"Hard disks";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:10:"Hard disks";}s:79:"Hard drive has children, <b>Writethrough</b> and <b>Shareable</b> not available";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:79:"Hard drive has children, <b>Writethrough</b> and <b>Shareable</b> not available";}s:86:"Hard drive is attached to a VM, <b>Immutable</b> and <b>Multi-attach</b> not available";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:86:"Hard drive is attached to a VM, <b>Immutable</b> and <b>Multi-attach</b> not available";}s:53:"Hard drive is dynamic, <b>Shareable</b> not available";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:53:"Hard drive is dynamic, <b>Shareable</b> not available";}s:128:"If you select <b>Delete</b> then the specified storage unit will be permanently deleted. This operation <b>cannot be undone</b>.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:128:"If you select <b>Delete</b> then the specified storage unit will be permanently deleted. This operation <b>cannot be undone</b>.";}s:215:"If you select <b>Keep</b> then the hard disk will be only removed from the list of known hard disks, but the storage unit will be left untouched which makes it possible to add this hard disk to the list later again.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:215:"If you select <b>Keep</b> then the hard disk will be only removed from the list of known hard disks, but the storage unit will be left untouched which makes it possible to add this hard disk to the list later again.";}s:9:"Immutable";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:9:"Immutable";}s:19:"Internal Networking";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:19:"Internal Networking";}s:3:"LUN";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:3:"LUN";}s:9:"Location:";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:9:"Location:";}s:18:"Medium attributes:";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:18:"Medium attributes:";}s:99:"Medium is attached to a VM that is in state "Running", "Paused", or "Saved". Unable to copy medium.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:99:"Medium is attached to a VM that is in state "Running", "Paused", or "Saved". Unable to copy medium.";}s:102:"Medium is attached to a VM that is in state "Running", "Paused", or "Saved". Unable to release medium.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:102:"Medium is attached to a VM that is in state "Running", "Paused", or "Saved". Unable to release medium.";}s:24:"Modify medium attributes";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:24:"Modify medium attributes";}s:9:"Modify...";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:9:"Modify...";}s:12:"Multi-Attach";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:12:"Multi-Attach";}s:11:"MultiAttach";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:11:"MultiAttach";}s:4:"Name";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:4:"Name";}s:3:"New";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:3:"New";}s:6:"Normal";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:6:"Normal";}s:113:"Note that the storage unit of this medium will not be deleted and that it will be possible to use it later again.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:113:"Note that the storage unit of this medium will not be deleted and that it will be possible to use it later again.";}s:13:"Optical disks";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:13:"Optical disks";}s:8:"Password";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:8:"Password";}s:95:"Please choose one of the following modes and press <b>%2</b> to proceed or <b>%3</b> otherwise.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:95:"Please choose one of the following modes and press <b>%2</b> to proceed or <b>%3</b> otherwise.";}s:4:"Port";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:4:"Port";}s:8:"Readonly";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:8:"Readonly";}s:7:"Refresh";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:7:"Refresh";}s:7:"Release";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:7:"Release";}s:6:"Remove";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:6:"Remove";}s:12:"Rename File:";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:12:"Rename File:";}s:6:"Select";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:6:"Select";}s:6:"Server";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:6:"Server";}s:9:"Shareable";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:9:"Shareable";}s:4:"Size";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:4:"Size";}s:16:"Storage details:";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:16:"Storage details:";}s:6:"Target";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:6:"Target";}s:69:"This will detach it from the following virtual machine(s): <b>%2</b>.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:69:"This will detach it from the following virtual machine(s): <b>%2</b>.";}s:5:"Type:";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:5:"Type:";}s:5:"UUID:";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:5:"UUID:";}s:8:"Username";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:8:"Username";}s:64:"VM hard drive is attached to is running, cannot modify disk type";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:64:"VM hard drive is attached to is running, cannot modify disk type";}s:21:"Virtual Media Manager";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:21:"Virtual Media Manager";}s:12:"Virtual Size";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:12:"Virtual Size";}s:7:"Warning";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:7:"Warning";}s:8:"Warnings";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:8:"Warnings";}s:12:"Writethrough";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:12:"Writethrough";}s:70:"You are about to change the settings of the disk image file <b>%1</b>.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:70:"You are about to change the settings of the disk image file <b>%1</b>.";}}}s:8:"UIWizard";a:1:{s:8:"messages";a:2:{s:11:"Expert Mode";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:11:"Expert Mode";}s:11:"Guided Mode";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:11:"Guided Mode";}}}s:15:"UIWizardCloneVM";a:1:{s:8:"messages";a:31:{s:8:"%1 Clone";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:8:"%1 Clone";}s:5:"Clone";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:5:"Clone";}s:13:"Clone Options";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:13:"Clone Options";}s:21:"Clone Virtual Machine";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:21:"Clone Virtual Machine";}s:10:"Clone type";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:10:"Clone type";}s:20:"Cloned Machine Name:";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:20:"Cloned Machine Name:";}s:21:"Current machine state";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:21:"Current machine state";}s:28:"Current snapshot tree branch";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:28:"Current snapshot tree branch";}s:10:"Everything";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:10:"Everything";}s:10:"Full Clone";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:10:"Full Clone";}s:51:"Generate new MAC addresses for all network adapters";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:51:"Generate new MAC addresses for all network adapters";}s:142:"If you choose <b>Current machine state</b>, the new machine will reflect the current state of the original machine and will have no snapshots.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:142:"If you choose <b>Current machine state</b>, the new machine will reflect the current state of the original machine and will have no snapshots.";}s:246:"If you choose <b>Current snapshot tree branch</b>, the new machine will reflect the current state of the original machine and will have matching snapshots for all snapshots in the tree branch starting at the current state in the original machine.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:246:"If you choose <b>Current snapshot tree branch</b>, the new machine will reflect the current state of the original machine and will have matching snapshots for all snapshots in the tree branch starting at the current state in the original machine.";}s:179:"If you choose <b>Everything</b>, the new machine will reflect the current state of the original machine and will have matching snapshots for all snapshots in the original machine.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:179:"If you choose <b>Everything</b>, the new machine will reflect the current state of the original machine and will have matching snapshots for all snapshots in the original machine.";}s:135:"If you choose <b>Full clone</b>, an exact copy (including all virtual hard disk files) of the original virtual machine will be created.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:135:"If you choose <b>Full clone</b>, an exact copy (including all virtual hard disk files) of the original virtual machine will be created.";}s:279:"If you choose <b>Linked clone</b>, a new machine will be created, but the virtual hard disk files will be tied to the virtual hard disk files of original machine and you will not be able to move the new virtual machine to a different computer without moving the original as well.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:279:"If you choose <b>Linked clone</b>, a new machine will be created, but the virtual hard disk files will be tied to the virtual hard disk files of original machine and you will not be able to move the new virtual machine to a different computer without moving the original as well.";}s:136:"If you create a <b>Linked clone</b>, then a new snapshot will be created in the original virtual machine as part of the cloning process.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:136:"If you create a <b>Linked clone</b>, then a new snapshot will be created in the original virtual machine as part of the cloning process.";}s:41:"Include all network adapter MAC addresses";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:41:"Include all network adapter MAC addresses";}s:46:"Include only NAT network adapter MAC addresses";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:46:"Include only NAT network adapter MAC addresses";}s:15:"Keep Disk Names";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:15:"Keep Disk Names";}s:19:"Keep Hardware UUIDs";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:19:"Keep Hardware UUIDs";}s:25:"Linked Base for %1 and %2";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:25:"Linked Base for %1 and %2";}s:12:"Linked Clone";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:12:"Linked Clone";}s:19:"MAC Address Policy:";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:19:"MAC Address Policy:";}s:16:"New machine name";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:16:"New machine name";}s:49:"Please choose a name for the new virtual machine.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:49:"Please choose a name for the new virtual machine.";}s:51:"Please choose the type of clone you wish to create.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:51:"Please choose the type of clone you wish to create.";}s:81:"Please choose which parts of the snapshot tree should be cloned with the machine.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:81:"Please choose which parts of the snapshot tree should be cloned with the machine.";}s:9:"Snapshots";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:9:"Snapshots";}s:57:"The new machine will be a clone of the machine <b>%1</b>.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:57:"The new machine will be a clone of the machine <b>%1</b>.";}s:9:"undefined";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:9:"undefined";}}}s:14:"UIWizardCopyVD";a:1:{s:8:"messages";a:19:{s:7:"%1_copy";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:7:"%1_copy";}s:219:"A <b>dynamically allocated</b> hard disk file will only use space on your physical hard disk as it fills up (up to a maximum <b>fixed size</b>), although it will not shrink again automatically when space on it is freed.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:219:"A <b>dynamically allocated</b> hard disk file will only use space on your physical hard disk as it fills up (up to a maximum <b>fixed size</b>), although it will not shrink again automatically when space on it is freed.";}s:104:"A <b>fixed size</b> hard disk file may take longer to create on some systems but is often faster to use.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:104:"A <b>fixed size</b> hard disk file may take longer to create on some systems but is often faster to use.";}s:42:"Choose a virtual hard disk file to copy...";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:42:"Choose a virtual hard disk file to copy...";}s:43:"Choose a virtual hard drive file to copy...";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:43:"Choose a virtual hard drive file to copy...";}s:4:"Copy";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:4:"Copy";}s:22:"Copy Virtual Hard Disk";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:22:"Copy Virtual Hard Disk";}s:21:"Dynamically allocated";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:21:"Dynamically allocated";}s:10:"Fixed size";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:10:"Fixed size";}s:19:"Hard disk file type";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:19:"Hard disk file type";}s:17:"Hard disk to copy";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:17:"Hard disk to copy";}s:23:"New hard disk to create";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:23:"New hard disk to create";}s:190:"Please choose the type of file that you would like to use for the new virtual hard disk. If you do not need to use it with other virtualization software you can leave this setting unchanged.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:190:"Please choose the type of file that you would like to use for the new virtual hard disk. If you do not need to use it with other virtualization software you can leave this setting unchanged.";}s:163:"Please choose whether the new virtual hard disk file should grow as it is used (dynamically allocated) or if it should be created at its maximum size (fixed size).";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:163:"Please choose whether the new virtual hard disk file should grow as it is used (dynamically allocated) or if it should be created at its maximum size (fixed size).";}s:193:"Please select the virtual hard disk file that you would like to copy if it is not already selected. You can either choose one from the list or use the folder icon beside the list to select one.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:193:"Please select the virtual hard disk file that you would like to copy if it is not already selected. You can either choose one from the list or use the folder icon beside the list to select one.";}s:153:"Please type the name of the new virtual hard disk file into the box below or click on the folder icon to select a different folder to create the file in.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:153:"Please type the name of the new virtual hard disk file into the box below or click on the folder icon to select a different folder to create the file in.";}s:33:"Split into files of less than 2GB";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:33:"Split into files of less than 2GB";}s:29:"Storage on physical hard disk";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:29:"Storage on physical hard disk";}s:252:"You can also choose to <b>split</b> the hard disk file into several files of up to two gigabytes each. This is mainly useful if you wish to store the virtual machine on removable USB devices or old systems, some of which cannot handle very large files.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:252:"You can also choose to <b>split</b> the hard disk file into several files of up to two gigabytes each. This is mainly useful if you wish to store the virtual machine on removable USB devices or old systems, some of which cannot handle very large files.";}}}s:17:"UIWizardExportApp";a:1:{s:8:"messages";a:28:{s:25:"Appliance Export Settings";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:25:"Appliance Export Settings";}s:18:"Appliance settings";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:18:"Appliance settings";}s:11:"Description";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:11:"Description";}s:6:"Export";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:6:"Export";}s:24:"Export Virtual Appliance";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:24:"Export Virtual Appliance";}s:5:"File:";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:5:"File:";}s:7:"Format:";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:7:"Format:";}s:116:"If you use an <b>ova</b> extension, then all the files will be combined into one Open Virtualization Format Archive.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:116:"If you use an <b>ova</b> extension, then all the files will be combined into one Open Virtualization Format Archive.";}s:77:"If you use an <b>ovf</b> extension, several files will be written separately.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:77:"If you use an <b>ovf</b> extension, several files will be written separately.";}s:7:"License";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:7:"License";}s:4:"Name";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:4:"Name";}s:7:"OVF 0.9";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:7:"OVF 0.9";}s:7:"OVF 1.0";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:7:"OVF 1.0";}s:7:"OVF 2.0";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:7:"OVF 2.0";}s:33:"Other extensions are not allowed.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:33:"Other extensions are not allowed.";}s:50:"Please choose a filename to export the OVF/OVA to.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:50:"Please choose a filename to export the OVF/OVA to.";}s:186:"Please select the virtual machines that should be added to the appliance. You can select more than one. Please note that these machines have to be turned off before they can be exported.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:186:"Please select the virtual machines that should be added to the appliance. You can select more than one. Please note that these machines have to be turned off before they can be exported.";}s:7:"Product";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:7:"Product";}s:11:"Product-URL";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:11:"Product-URL";}s:16:"Restore Defaults";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:16:"Restore Defaults";}s:33:"Select a directory to export into";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:33:"Select a directory to export into";}s:140:"This is the descriptive information which will be added to the virtual appliance.  You can change it by double clicking on individual lines.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:140:"This is the descriptive information which will be added to the virtual appliance.  You can change it by double clicking on individual lines.";}s:6:"Vendor";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:6:"Vendor";}s:10:"Vendor-URL";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:10:"Vendor-URL";}s:7:"Version";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:7:"Version";}s:26:"Virtual machines to export";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:26:"Virtual machines to export";}s:19:"Write Manifest file";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:19:"Write Manifest file";}s:9:"undefined";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:9:"undefined";}}}s:16:"UIWizardFirstRun";a:1:{s:8:"messages";a:6:{s:37:"Choose a virtual optical disk file...";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:37:"Choose a virtual optical disk file...";}s:127:"Please select a virtual optical disk file or a physical optical drive containing a disk to start your new virtual machine from.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:127:"Please select a virtual optical disk file or a physical optical drive containing a disk to start your new virtual machine from.";}s:20:"Select start-up disk";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:20:"Select start-up disk";}s:5:"Start";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:5:"Start";}s:343:"The disk should be suitable for starting a computer from and should contain the operating system you wish to install on the virtual machine if you want to do that now. The disk will be ejected from the virtual drive automatically next time you switch the virtual machine off, but you can also do this yourself if needed using the Devices menu.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:343:"The disk should be suitable for starting a computer from and should contain the operating system you wish to install on the virtual machine if you want to do that now. The disk will be ejected from the virtual drive automatically next time you switch the virtual machine off, but you can also do this yourself if needed using the Devices menu.";}s:172:"The disk should be suitable for starting a computer from. As this virtual machine has no hard drive you will not be able to install an operating system on it at the moment.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:172:"The disk should be suitable for starting a computer from. As this virtual machine has no hard drive you will not be able to install an operating system on it at the moment.";}}}s:17:"UIWizardImportApp";a:1:{s:8:"messages";a:28:{s:18:"Appliance settings";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:18:"Appliance settings";}s:19:"Appliance to import";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:19:"Appliance to import";}s:3:"CPU";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:3:"CPU";}s:44:"Choose a virtual appliance file to import...";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:44:"Choose a virtual appliance file to import...";}s:3:"DVD";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:3:"DVD";}s:6:"Floppy";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:6:"Floppy";}s:13:"Guest OS Type";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:13:"Guest OS Type";}s:6:"Import";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:6:"Import";}s:24:"Import Virtual Appliance";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:24:"Import Virtual Appliance";}s:4:"Name";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:4:"Name";}s:15:"Network Adapter";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:15:"Network Adapter";}s:3:"RAM";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:3:"RAM";}s:49:"Reinitialize the MAC address of all network cards";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:49:"Reinitialize the MAC address of all network cards";}s:16:"Restore Defaults";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:16:"Restore Defaults";}s:29:"Select an appliance to import";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:29:"Select an appliance to import";}s:10:"Sound Card";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:10:"Sound Card";}s:24:"Storage Controller (IDE)";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:24:"Storage Controller (IDE)";}s:25:"Storage Controller (PCIe)";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:25:"Storage Controller (PCIe)";}s:24:"Storage Controller (SAS)";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:24:"Storage Controller (SAS)";}s:25:"Storage Controller (SATA)";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:25:"Storage Controller (SATA)";}s:25:"Storage Controller (SCSI)";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:25:"Storage Controller (SCSI)";}s:31:"Storage Controller (VirtioSCSI)";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:31:"Storage Controller (VirtioSCSI)";}s:245:"These are the virtual machines contained in the appliance and the suggested settings of the imported VirtualBox machines. You can change many of the properties shown by double-clicking on the items and disable others using the check boxes below.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:245:"These are the virtual machines contained in the appliance and the suggested settings of the imported VirtualBox machines. You can change many of the properties shown by double-clicking on the items and disable others using the check boxes below.";}s:14:"USB Controller";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:14:"USB Controller";}s:18:"Virtual Disk Image";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:18:"Virtual Disk Image";}s:17:"Virtual System %1";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:17:"Virtual System %1";}s:143:"VirtualBox currently supports importing appliances saved in the Open Virtualization Format (OVF). To continue, select the file to import below.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:143:"VirtualBox currently supports importing appliances saved in the Open Virtualization Format (OVF). To continue, select the file to import below.";}s:9:"Warnings:";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:9:"Warnings:";}}}s:13:"UIWizardNewVD";a:1:{s:8:"messages";a:27:{s:219:"A <b>dynamically allocated</b> hard disk file will only use space on your physical hard disk as it fills up (up to a maximum <b>fixed size</b>), although it will not shrink again automatically when space on it is freed.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:219:"A <b>dynamically allocated</b> hard disk file will only use space on your physical hard disk as it fills up (up to a maximum <b>fixed size</b>), although it will not shrink again automatically when space on it is freed.";}s:104:"A <b>fixed size</b> hard disk file may take longer to create on some systems but is often faster to use.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:104:"A <b>fixed size</b> hard disk file may take longer to create on some systems but is often faster to use.";}s:51:"Choose a location for new virtual hard disk file...";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:51:"Choose a location for new virtual hard disk file...";}s:52:"Choose a location for new virtual hard drive file...";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:52:"Choose a location for new virtual hard drive file...";}s:6:"Create";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:6:"Create";}s:24:"Create Virtual Hard Disk";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:24:"Create Virtual Hard Disk";}s:21:"Dynamically allocated";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:21:"Dynamically allocated";}s:13:"File location";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:13:"File location";}s:22:"File location and size";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:22:"File location and size";}s:9:"File size";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:9:"File size";}s:10:"Fixed size";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:10:"Fixed size";}s:25:"HDD (Parallels Hard Disk)";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:25:"HDD (Parallels Hard Disk)";}s:19:"Hard disk file type";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:19:"Hard disk file type";}s:8:"Location";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:8:"Location";}s:190:"Please choose the type of file that you would like to use for the new virtual hard disk. If you do not need to use it with other virtualization software you can leave this setting unchanged.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:190:"Please choose the type of file that you would like to use for the new virtual hard disk. If you do not need to use it with other virtualization software you can leave this setting unchanged.";}s:163:"Please choose whether the new virtual hard disk file should grow as it is used (dynamically allocated) or if it should be created at its maximum size (fixed size).";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:163:"Please choose whether the new virtual hard disk file should grow as it is used (dynamically allocated) or if it should be created at its maximum size (fixed size).";}s:153:"Please type the name of the new virtual hard disk file into the box below or click on the folder icon to select a different folder to create the file in.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:153:"Please type the name of the new virtual hard disk file into the box below or click on the folder icon to select a different folder to create the file in.";}s:25:"QCOW (QEMU Copy-On-Write)";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:25:"QCOW (QEMU Copy-On-Write)";}s:24:"QED (QEMU enhanced disk)";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:24:"QED (QEMU enhanced disk)";}s:167:"Select the size of the virtual hard disk in megabytes. This size is the limit on the amount of file data that a virtual machine will be able to store on the hard disk.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:167:"Select the size of the virtual hard disk in megabytes. This size is the limit on the amount of file data that a virtual machine will be able to store on the hard disk.";}s:33:"Split into files of less than 2GB";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:33:"Split into files of less than 2GB";}s:29:"Storage on physical hard disk";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:29:"Storage on physical hard disk";}s:27:"VDI (VirtualBox Disk Image)";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:27:"VDI (VirtualBox Disk Image)";}s:23:"VHD (Virtual Hard Disk)";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:23:"VHD (Virtual Hard Disk)";}s:27:"VMDK (Virtual Machine Disk)";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:27:"VMDK (Virtual Machine Disk)";}s:252:"You can also choose to <b>split</b> the hard disk file into several files of up to two gigabytes each. This is mainly useful if you wish to store the virtual machine on removable USB devices or old systems, some of which cannot handle very large files.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:252:"You can also choose to <b>split</b> the hard disk file into several files of up to two gigabytes each. This is mainly useful if you wish to store the virtual machine on removable USB devices or old systems, some of which cannot handle very large files.";}s:9:"undefined";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:9:"undefined";}}}s:13:"UIWizardNewVM";a:1:{s:8:"messages";a:18:{s:6:"Create";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:6:"Create";}s:22:"Create Virtual Machine";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:22:"Create Virtual Machine";}s:30:"Create a virtual hard disk now";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:30:"Create a virtual hard disk now";}s:30:"Do not add a virtual hard disk";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:30:"Do not add a virtual hard disk";}s:9:"Hard disk";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:9:"Hard disk";}s:138:"If you need a more complex storage set-up you can skip this step and make the changes to the machine settings once the machine is created.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:138:"If you need a more complex storage set-up you can skip this step and make the changes to the machine settings once the machine is created.";}s:63:"If you wish you can add a virtual hard disk to the new machine.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:63:"If you wish you can add a virtual hard disk to the new machine.";}s:11:"Memory size";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:11:"Memory size";}s:25:"Name and operating system";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:25:"Name and operating system";}s:5:"Name:";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:5:"Name:";}s:210:"Please choose a descriptive name for the new virtual machine and select the type of operating system you intend to install on it. The name you choose will be used throughout VirtualBox to identify this machine.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:210:"Please choose a descriptive name for the new virtual machine and select the type of operating system you intend to install on it. The name you choose will be used throughout VirtualBox to identify this machine.";}s:86:"Select the amount of memory (RAM) in megabytes to be allocated to the virtual machine.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:86:"Select the amount of memory (RAM) in megabytes to be allocated to the virtual machine.";}s:44:"The recommended memory size is <b>%1 MB</b>.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:44:"The recommended memory size is <b>%1 MB</b>.";}s:51:"The recommended size of the hard disk is <b>%1</b>.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:51:"The recommended size of the hard disk is <b>%1</b>.";}s:5:"Type:";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:5:"Type:";}s:38:"Use an existing virtual hard disk file";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:38:"Use an existing virtual hard disk file";}s:8:"Version:";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:8:"Version:";}s:118:"You can either create a new hard disk file or select one from the list or from another location using the folder icon.";a:1:{s:11:"translation";s:118:"You can either create a new hard disk file or select one from the list or from another location using the folder icon.";}}}}}